  'set.subTmpl': 'Subscription formats and templates', 'set.subAutoFormat': 'Pick the format by client', 'set.subAutoFormatHelp': 'The universal link (no format) looks at the client: official sing-box apps (SFA / SFI / SFM / SFW / SFL) and godusevpn get JSON; Clash-family apps get YAML; NekoBox, Throne, Hiddify, v2rayN, Shadowrocket and similar get share links. Legacy Clash cores (CFW / ClashX / CFA) never receive protocols they cannot parse or SS-2022, even with format=clash; add format=mihomo to force the new core. Links with an explicit format are not affected by this switch',
  'set.subClashExt': 'Clash template (YAML, empty = built-in)', 'set.subClashExtHelp': 'Write DNS, rules and your own groups; the panel fills in the nodes and the Proxy / Auto groups, plus a url-test group named after each line deployed on several servers (a number is added on a name clash). A group with the same name uses yours. Use include-all: true in a group to take every node. The ipv6 switch is turned on when the subscription has nodes with IPv6 addresses', 'set.clashIPv6Hint': 'The Clash template sets ipv6: false. When the subscription has nodes with IPv6 addresses, the generated config switches it to ipv6: true; with it off, mihomo cannot connect to those nodes.',
  'set.subSingboxExt': 'sing-box template (JSON, empty = built-in)', 'set.subSingboxExtHelp': 'Sections you write (dns, route, inbounds…) are used as they are, the rest come from the built-in one. Nodes are appended to outbounds, "{all}" in a selector / urltest expands to every node (not the line groups); proxy / auto / direct are added if missing. Each line deployed on several servers also gets a urltest group named after it: a selector / urltest of the same name in your template is used instead, any other name clash adds a number',
