  'set.subPageTitle': 'Page title', 'set.subPageTitleHelp': 'Empty = profile title',
  'set.subPageSupport': 'Footer contact', 'set.subPageNotice': 'Notice (multi-line)',
  'set.subPageSupportHelp': 'Links allowed: text(https://…) shows only the text; half- or full-width parentheses, and a space before them is fine. The link text runs back from the parenthesis to the nearest punctuation, link or auto-detected handle. Tg: @username and WhatsApp: +number become clickable links automatically.',
  'set.subPageNoticeHelp': 'Links allowed: text(https://…) or [text](https://…) shows only the text (half- or full-width brackets); Tg: @username and WhatsApp: +number become links automatically. Only http(s), tg, mailto and tel links. In text(link) the text runs back from the parenthesis to the nearest punctuation or previous link; use [text](link) when the text contains a / or the link contains parentheses.',
  'set.subPageLogo': 'Landing page logo',
  'set.logoHelp': 'Takes effect on upload, no need to save. PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP or SVG; the browser first shrinks it to fit 480×160 and converts it to PNG (64 KB at most). Shown 28 px tall and at most 160 px wide on landing pages, and used as the browser tab icon. Landing pages follow the visitor’s dark mode and put a light backdrop behind the logo there; the preview above shows both. A white logo on a transparent background is hard to see in either, so use a dark one or one with its own background.',
