  'set.logoNode': 'On a node the logo follows the master; change it in the master panel',
  'set.subPageBuyURL': 'Purchase / renew link', 'set.subPageBuyURLHelp': 'When set, landing pages show a “Purchase / renew” button (the main button once a subscription is expired, exhausted or disabled) and so does the “invalid link” page; http:// or https:// only. Resellers can set their own in their panel; empty falls back to this one.',
  'set.trustedProxies': 'Trusted reverse proxies', 'set.trustedProxiesHelp': 'If the panel, reseller panel or external API sits behind a reverse proxy (Nginx, Caddy, ...), enter the proxy addresses, e.g. 127.0.0.1, ::1; separate several with commas, CIDR ranges allowed. Login and external API failure limits then take the client from X-Forwarded-For (the rightmost address not in this list) or X-Real-IP; otherwise every caller looks like the proxy and ten bad attempts from anyone lock everyone out. The proxy must append or overwrite that header. Leave empty without a proxy (only the connecting peer counts). Takes effect on save, no restart needed.',
  'set.supportOnline': 'Supporters list and online panel count', 'set.supportOnlineHelp': 'm-ui has no telemetry. When on, the Feedback page reads the supporters list online and the panel downloads an empty file from GitHub once a day to count online panels, with no identifier. When off, all of this stops and the page no longer shows them.',
  'nav.rules': 'Rules', 'rule.title': 'Rules', 'rule.subtitle': 'Temporary speed limits by time of day or burst usage. The master evaluates rules and syncs them to every node; when the condition ends (outside the window, penalty expired, rule disabled) users fall back to their own limits.',
