  'reach.v6.s.ok': 'open', 'reach.v6.s.down': 'blocked', 'reach.v6.s.unsure': 'unclear', 'reach.v6.s.udp': 'UDP lines only', 'reach.v6.s.none': 'no probes', 'reach.v6.s.error': 'check failed', 'reach.v6.s.udpLine': 'not tested (UDP)', 'reach.v6.s.otherPort': 'port not tested',
  'reach.v6.x.ok': 'Mainland home-network probes with IPv6 can connect to {addr}: this server is reachable over IPv6 from mainland China.',
  'reach.v6.x.down': 'Neither mainland probes nor probes abroad can connect to {addr}: most likely the cloud security group does not allow this port for ::/0, or ip6tables / nftables / ufw on the server blocks IPv6; the IPv6 may also be outbound-only (WARP, NAT66, egress-only gateway).',
  'reach.v6.x.unsure': 'Too few probes reached {addr} to tell; check again later.',
  'reach.v6.x.none': 'No IPv6-capable probes were available this time; try again later.',
  'reach.v6.x.error': 'The check did not complete: {err}',
  'reach.v6.x.udp': 'All IPv6 lines on this server are UDP ({lines}) and probes can only connect over TCP, so they cannot be tested: run tcpdump -ni any ip6 and udp port <port> on the server (with port hopping capture the range too: tcpdump -ni any "ip6 and (udp port <port> or udp portrange <from>-<to>)") and connect once from a client. No packets at all means the cloud security group, routing or the client network; packets in but none out: on hysteria2 with obfuscation check the client\'s obfuscation password first (with a wrong one the server drops packets silently, just like a firewall), then the server firewall, or replies leaving through the wrong route.',
  'reach.v6.portOf': 'Tested port {port} of line "{name}".', 'reach.v6.udpAlso': 'UDP lines {lines} cannot be tested; capture packets to confirm.',
  'reach.v6.attempt': 'The latest check ({t}) did not complete: {err}; showing the previous result.', 'reach.v6.attemptNone': 'The latest check ({t}) had no IPv6-capable probes; showing the previous result.', 'reach.v6.lineUdp': 'This line uses UDP (hysteria2 / tuic) and probes can only connect over TCP, so it cannot be tested: run tcpdump -ni any ip6 and udp port {port} on the server (with port hopping capture the range too: tcpdump -ni any "ip6 and (udp port <port> or udp portrange <from>-<to>)"), connect once from a client and see whether packets come in and replies go out; packets in but none out on hysteria2 with obfuscation: check the client\'s obfuscation password first (with a wrong one the server drops packets silently). Both the cloud security group and the server firewall must allow UDP from ::/0 separately (the whole range with port hopping).', 'reach.v6.lineOther': 'This IPv6 inbound check tested port {tport} of line "{name}" (result: {s}), not this line\'s port {port}: only the first TCP line using IPv6 is tested on each server. The security group and firewall must allow ::/0 on each port separately, so another port being open says nothing about this one.', 'reach.v6.lineNoTcp': 'At the last IPv6 inbound check all IPv6 lines on this server were UDP, so this line\'s port {port} was not tested; the next round will test it.',
  'reach.v6.note': 'When a subscription serves lines over IPv6, this address is checked in the same round as the mainland check: first from Globalping home-network probes in mainland China that have IPv6 (about 4 probe credits); if none of them connects, or no mainland IPv6 probe is available this time, probes abroad (Europe and North America, about 4) are asked too, to tell a closed inbound from an address that is unreachable from the mainland. The mainland check gets the quota first and this uses what is left; no extra schedule. Only the port of the first TCP line served over IPv6 is tested on each server, other ports must be opened separately; UDP lines cannot be tested.',
  'reach.v6TcpOnly': 'All TCP lines on this server use IPv6 in subscriptions and their ports must not be used to test the IPv4 address, so the IPv4 check used this port: when Hong Kong probes can connect it shows whether the IP is blocked; when the panel API port is open to the master only and Hong Kong cannot connect either, the result is "No testable port" with no alert. For the IPv6 path see IPv6 inbound below.',
  'reach.v6TcpOnlySub': 'All TCP lines on this server use IPv6 in subscriptions and their ports must not be used to test the IPv4 address, so the IPv4 check used the subscription port: it shows whether the IPv4 of the subscription address is blocked — users refresh their subscriptions through it, and when it is blocked users in mainland China cannot get new nodes. For the IPv6 path see IPv6 inbound below.',
  'set.reach': 'Mainland reachability', 'set.reachAuto': 'Automatic checks',
  'set.reachAutoHelp': 'Periodically checks every server from China Mobile, China Telecom and China Unicom home-broadband probes (no data-center probes) and sends a Telegram alert when one gets blocked or recovers. Server addresses are sent to the public Globalping network.',
  'set.reachMinutes': 'Interval (minutes)', 'set.reachMinutesHelp': 'Default 90, 30–1440 allowed. One server uses about 15 probe runs, plus about 4 for servers with IPv6 lines (IPv6 inbound, which only gets what the mainland checks leave over); Globalping allows about 250 per hour without an account, counted per master IP.',
  'set.reachToken': 'Globalping token (optional)', 'set.reachTokenHelp': 'Create one for free at globalping.io for a higher limit; empty = the anonymous limit of the master IP.',
