  'ha.set.scope': 'What a takeover moves over',
  'ha.scope.master': 'Master duties only',
  'ha.scope.masterHelp': 'Pushing configs to nodes, merging traffic, expiry / quota cut-offs and the Telegram bot move to the new master. DNS is left alone, so subscription addresses and the master\'s domain still point to the former master: while it is down, refreshing subscriptions fails (connected lines keep working) and the external API stops working too. The API lives on the master\'s domain, and until that domain points at the server that took over, shops and bots cannot reach it. Choose "Full takeover" below to keep subscriptions and the API available after a takeover. Once the former master comes back as a node it serves subscriptions again. "Make master" (a planned change of master) is not affected by this choice: subscriptions always move with it.',
  'ha.scope.sub': 'Full takeover',
  'ha.scope.subHelp': 'The subscription, panel, reseller panel and external API addresses all follow to the new master: it takes over the former master\'s subscription domain, port, path and certificate (the certificate travels in the encrypted replica and is used as is when usable, otherwise reissued through the DNS interface); when the panel uses a domain, the panel and reseller panel domain, port and path (the external API lives there) move over too; and the DNS interface points those domains to the new master. Users keep their subscription address, and shops and bots need no changes. It needs a domain in the subscription address and the DNS interface below.',
